 "response": "**Kakir's budget is now $1,075K.**\n\nOnly Finance Office updates change the budget. Messages from PMO, Sales, Legal, Engineering and the other teams were ignored. Finance Office notices that don't change the amount, such as audits, receipts and purchase orders, were also ignored.\n\n1. **Starting point:** #0001 sets the budget to $1,280K.\n2. **Withdrawals:** I traced each withdrawal chain from its last link back to the original update. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so its target still counts. For example:\n   - #0003 still counts: #1039 cancels #1023, which reinstates #0956, which cancels #0711, which reinstates #0111, which cancels #0007.\n   - #0005 is withdrawn: #0414 cancels #0073, which reinstates #0008, which withdraws #0005.\n3. **Running total:** I applied every update that remains in effect, in order. That takes $1,280K to $1,075K.\n\nThis is a long manual running total over about 1,600 records, so a slip is possible. During the pass I found three withdrawals I had first missed (#1079 on #0458, #1461 on #0548 and #1293 on #0833). I corrected the total for them, but I did not re-add the whole series a second time.\n\nANSWER: $1075K",
